                                    <h1>Jewelry Product Photography — 360&amp;deg; + Zoom + AR + Video for D2C (2026) | ITD GrowthLabs</h1>
                                    <div style="background:#fff7ed;border-left:4px solid #ff5722;padding:20px 24px;border-radius:10px;margin:24px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#334155;"><strong style="color:#ea580c;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:0.4px;">ITD JEWELRY PORTFOLIO &mdash; THE EVIDENCE:</strong><br>This article is written from live jewelry vertical work. ITD GrowthLabs is a specialist <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-jewelry-brands.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">digital marketing agency for jewelry brands</a> with a delivered <a href="/resources/Fabelia_Jewelry_D2C_Marketing_Strategy_Case_Study_2026.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Fabelia jewelry D2C case study</a>, 8+ published jewelry playbooks including <a href="/resources/Gold_vs_Diamond_Jewelry_D2C_Strategy_2026.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Gold vs Diamond D2C Strategy</a>, <a href="/resources/Jewelry_D2C_Digital_Transformation_India_Dubai_2026.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Jewelry D2C Digital Transformation India + Dubai</a>, <a href="/resources/Best_D2C_Jewellery_Brands_UAE_GCC_2026_2027.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Best D2C Jewellery Brands UAE + GCC</a>, and city-specific jewelry marketing pages across <a href="/services/gcc/dubai-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Dubai</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/abu-dhabi-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Abu Dhabi</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/jeddah-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Jeddah</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/doha-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Doha</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/dammam-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Dammam</a>, and <a href="/services/gcc/al-khobar-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Al Khobar</a>. Every framework below is grounded in live category work &mdash; not generic D2C theory.</div><p>Jewelry photography is where D2C conversion is won or lost. Static-only photos crater conversion 30-60% below category norm. Poor lighting or missing angles trigger doubt in high-value buyers. Skimping here to save Rs 30K in launch budget costs Rs 3-8 lakh in lost revenue over 12 months.</p><p>This piece maps the full jewelry photography + video + AR asset production framework &mdash; what each SKU needs, studio setup, realistic cost, and the workflow that ships 50-100 SKUs / week without quality drop.</p>
                                    <h2>What every jewelry SKU needs (the 8-shot spec)</h2>
                                    <p>Category-standard SKU shot list for D2C jewelry:</p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Hero front-facing:</strong> On white background, sharp focus, minimal shadow. Primary catalog thumbnail.</li><li><strong>360&deg; spin:</strong> 24-32 frames rotating on turntable. Interactive JS on product page.</li><li><strong>Macro / zoom detail:</strong> Hallmark stamp, stone setting, prong finishing, chain link, clasp. Trust signal.</li><li><strong>Side + back:</strong> Depth + finishing quality visible.</li><li><strong>Scale reference:</strong> On coin, ruler, or hand. Buyers overestimate size online without reference.</li><li><strong>On-model:</strong> Ring on hand, earring on ear, necklace on neck, bracelet on wrist. Real skin + light + drape.</li><li><strong>Lifestyle:</strong> Piece in context (bridal, festive, everyday). Emotional trigger.</li><li><strong>15-30 second video:</strong> Multi-angle + on-model + light-play + text overlays of key specs.</li></ul><p>Add for rings + earrings + necklaces: <strong>AR-ready 3D scan</strong> (see <a href="/resources/jewelry_try_on_ar_ai_tools_d2c.php">AR try-on playbook</a>).</p>
                                    <h2>Studio setup + equipment</h2>
                                    <p>Serious jewelry photography setup for in-house or contracted studio:</p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Camera:</strong> Sony A7R V or Canon R5 (60MP+ for macro detail). Rs 3-5 lakh.</li><li><strong>Macro lens:</strong> 90mm or 100mm macro. Rs 60K-Rs 1.2 lakh.</li><li><strong>Continuous LED lighting:</strong> 2-4 panel setup with softboxes. Rs 60K-Rs 1.5 lakh. Godox SL-60 or Aputure 300D popular.</li><li><strong>Turntable + rig:</strong> Motorised 360&deg; turntable + camera trigger. Rs 30-80K. WebRotate + Ortery brands.</li><li><strong>Light tent + backgrounds:</strong> White + black + gradient + colored acrylic surfaces. Rs 15-40K.</li><li><strong>Colour reference tools:</strong> X-Rite ColorChecker + Pantone reference. Rs 8-15K.</li><li><strong>Editing station:</strong> Mac Studio or high-spec PC + calibrated monitor. Rs 2-4 lakh.</li></ul><p>Total in-house studio setup: Rs 8-18 lakh. Contracted studio day-rate Rs 25-80K depending on city + specialist.</p>
                                    <h2>Per-SKU cost benchmarks</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Contracted studio (Mumbai / Delhi / Bengaluru + top-tier):</strong> Rs 1,500-4,500 per SKU (8-shot + video + edit + AR-ready 3D scan). Rs 800-1,800 per SKU for basic shot-list.</p><p><strong>Contracted studio (Tier 2 cities):</strong> Rs 600-1,500 per SKU. Quality varies significantly &mdash; do sample shoot before committing.</p><p><strong>Contracted studio (Dubai):</strong> AED 200-600 per SKU (Rs 4,400-13,200). Higher rates but strong for Arabic-market shoots.</p><p><strong>In-house studio (once fixed cost recovered):</strong> Rs 200-500 marginal cost per SKU. Justified at 50+ SKU / month volume.</p><p><strong>AI-augmented workflow:</strong> Photograph 3-5 canonical shots per SKU + use AI (Photoroom, Cloudinary, Descript) for background swaps + variant renders. Cuts cost 30-50% + speeds output 3-5x. Full AI-generated jewelry photography still unreliable for high-value + trust-critical shots.</p>
                                    <h2>Workflow &amp;mdash; shipping 50-100 SKUs / week</h2>
                                    <p>Batch photography workflow that ships high volume without quality drop:</p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Day 1 pre-production:</strong> SKU sheet with dimensions + gemstone + hallmark position + shot-list per SKU. Wardrobe + hand + model briefing.</li><li><strong>Day 2-3 shoot:</strong> Batch by category (all rings first, all earrings next, all necklaces last). 25-40 SKUs / day per photographer. Turntable + macro + on-model + lifestyle in parallel setups.</li><li><strong>Day 4-5 editing:</strong> Batch RAW &rarr; retoucher &rarr; QA. Colour-calibrated monitor. Consistent LUT + finishing across batch.</li><li><strong>Day 6 QA + upload:</strong> Shopify upload with alt-text + metadata + AR-ready 3D scan flagged for asset prep.</li><li><strong>Day 7 buffer:</strong> Reshoots + corrections + edge cases.</li></ul><p>Monthly output 100-300 SKUs / month for a serious in-house or dedicated-agency setup.</p>
                                    <h2>Video &amp;mdash; the underused conversion lever</h2>
                                    <p>Video content converts 2-4x higher than static-only on jewelry SKU pages. Types that work:</p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>15-30 second SKU video:</strong> Multi-angle + on-model + light-play + spec overlay. On every SKU page.</li><li><strong>60-90 second collection story:</strong> Design inspiration + craftsmanship + on-model. Collection landing pages + Instagram + Reels.</li><li><strong>3-5 minute founder + designer walk-through:</strong> Behind-the-scenes + storytelling. YouTube + brand pages.</li><li><strong>Live Shopping video (30-60 min):</strong> Weekly Instagram + Facebook Live. Bridal + festive activation.</li><li><strong>Certification walkthrough (60-120 sec):</strong> "How to read your BIS + IGI certificate." Trust signal + educational SEO.</li></ul><p>Total video budget: Rs 1.5-4 lakh / quarter for a serious content pipeline. Amortises across 3-6 months of amplification.</p>

                                    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%); padding: 40px; border-radius: 12px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; color: #fff;">
                                        <h3 style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:15px;">Ready to Get Started?</h3>
                                        <p style="color:#ccc;margin-bottom:25px;">Book a free 30-minute jewelry D2C discovery call. We map your brand + funnel + share a customised proposal within 3 working days.</p>
                                        <a href="https://www.itdgrowthlabs.com/contact-us.php" style="background:#ff5722;color:#fff;padding:14px 32px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;display:inline-block;margin-right:10px;">Contact Us Today</a>
                                        <a href="https://calendly.com/itdgrowthlabs-info/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="js-book-call" data-source="blog_cta" style="background:#1565c0;color:#fff;padding:14px 32px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;display:inline-block;">Book Free 30-min Call</a>
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How much does jewelry product photography cost per SKU?</h3>
                                        <p>Rs 1,500-4,500 per SKU for full 8-shot + video + edit + AR-ready 3D scan (Mumbai / Delhi / Bengaluru top-tier). Rs 800-1,800 for basic shot-list. Rs 600-1,500 in tier-2 cities (quality varies). AED 200-600 in Dubai. Rs 200-500 marginal in-house.</p>
                                        <h3>What shots does every jewelry SKU need?</h3>
                                        <p>Hero front, 360&deg; spin (24-32 frames), macro / zoom detail (hallmark + stone setting), side + back, scale reference, on-model, lifestyle context, 15-30 second video. AR-ready 3D scan for rings + earrings + necklaces.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I build an in-house jewelry photography studio?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes at 50+ SKU / month sustained volume. Fixed cost Rs 8-18 lakh setup, marginal Rs 200-500 per SKU. Below 50 SKU / month, contracted studio + AI-augmented workflow is more cost-efficient.</p>
                                        <h3>Can AI generate jewelry photography?</h3>
                                        <p>Partially. AI-augmented workflow (canonical shots + AI background swaps + variant renders via Photoroom, Cloudinary, Descript) cuts cost 30-50% + speeds output 3-5x. Full AI-generated jewelry photography still unreliable for high-value + trust-critical shots.</p>
                                        <h3>How much video content does a jewelry brand need per month?</h3>
                                        <p>15-30 second video on every SKU. 60-90 second collection story per new collection. 3-5 minute founder walk-through monthly. 30-60 minute Live Shopping weekly. Total Rs 1.5-4 lakh / quarter for serious pipeline.</p>
                                        <h3>What editing + retouching standards matter?</h3>
                                        <p>Colour-calibrated monitor + X-Rite ColorChecker reference during shoot. Consistent LUT across batch. Retoucher trained on jewelry (hallmark preservation, stone brilliance, prong-detail, chain-link clarity). QA against reference SKU per batch.</p>
                                        <h3>Do we need a photographer specialist or can generic e-com photographer work?</h3>
                                        <p>Specialist for fine + bridal + luxury. Generic e-com photographer misses macro + hallmark + certification detail. Specialist charges 30-70% premium but delivers 2-3x conversion lift on SKU pages vs generic e-com. See our <a href="/resources/jewelry_photographer_video_specialist_agency_india.php">jewelry photographer agency checklist</a>.</p>
                                        <h3>How does ITD GrowthLabs handle jewelry photography for clients?</h3>
                                        <p>In-house pod for Growth-tier + Enterprise clients. Photographer + retoucher + video editor trained on jewelry-specific requirements. Batch workflow shipping 100-300 SKUs / month per client. AR-ready 3D scans + video + on-model in parallel. See our <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-jewelry-brands.php">jewelry vertical page</a>.</p>
